WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:21.270
If a person has severe arthritis of the ankle,
a doctor may recommend a surgical procedure

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:30.120
called ankle arthroplasty, or total ankle
replacement.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.700
The ankle is the joint that connects the leg
and the foot.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:43.590
The ankle joint includes the two lower leg
bones, called the tibia and the fibula, and

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:47.079
the ankle bone, called the talus.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:58.110
The joint allows the foot to move up and down.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:04.080
On the ends of the bones is a smooth gliding
covering called articular cartilage.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.960
Sometimes the ankle can become damaged from
injury, or normal wear and tear, or other

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:10.960
diseases.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:17.740
This can result in arthritis, which is painful
joint inflammation and stiffness.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:24.729
Over time the articular cartilage can wear
away, causing the exposed bony surfaces to

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:27.829
rub together.

00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:33.810
In addition, arthritis can lead to changes
in the shape of the bones of the ankle joint.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:40.369
For example, boney projections, called bone
spurs, can develop.

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:49.020
The bone spurs, along with the damaged cartilage,
can make it hard to move the foot up and down.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:55.749
As a result, it can be difficult to walk and
go up and down stairs.

00:01:55.749 --> 00:02:04.249
Two types of arthritis that can affect the
ankle joint are osteoarthritis due to wear

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:11.770
and tear on the joint or injury, and rheumatoid
arthritis, one of several autoimmune disorders

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.880
that causes inflammation in the joint.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:23.670
A surgical procedure called total ankle replacement
is done to replace a severely damaged ankle

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.720
joint.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:32.930
The surgeon will make an incision on the front
of the damaged ankle to reveal the ankle joint.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:39.340
Next, the ends of the tibia and the talus
will be removed.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:50.810
A man made joint called an implant or a prosthesis
will be inserted into the ankle.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:58.319
At the end of the procedure the incision will
be closed with stitches.

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:03.439
After ankle replacement the patient will be
able to move the ankle more fully and experience

00:03:03.439 --> 00:03:05.170
less pain during activity.

